-- ind-c-tests-simplex.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of the SimpLEX test table (Figure 4; rows 5 to 8 and the
-- worked example), run against the three vintages.  Expected outcomes are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md
-- section J, decided from the screenshot and the regulations before the encoding was opened:
--   row 5, theoretical exam (paid):           draft approved; as made approved (no fee at all); as amended approved
--   row 6, practical exam (paid):             approved in all three
--   row 7, appeal paying 40:                  examined in all three
--   row 8, an exam without payment:           practical: refused in all three; theoretical: refused in the draft and
--                                             as amended, NOT refused as made (no fee is fixed for it)
--   the worked example (theoretical, unpaid): draft rejected; as made NOT rejected; as amended rejected
-- The draft's regulation 4 is not on the screenshot; the worked example itself says what it does ("reg 4 forbids
-- registration without payment").  The tests here take that reading for the draft (the encoding's alternative,
-- `the SimpLEX reading that takes the draft's regulation 4 as regulation 4 as made`); what the encoding's own
-- reading does with the draft is in ind-c-tests-ambiguous.l4.

§ `ind-c: the SimpLEX table`

§§ `Fixtures`

`draft` MEANS `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`
`as made` MEANS `the Fees Regulations as made`
`as amended` MEANS `the Fees Regulations as amended`
`taken` MEANS `the SimpLEX reading that the encoding takes`
`draft reg 4 as made` MEANS `the SimpLEX reading that takes the draft's regulation 4 as regulation 4 as made`
`not barred` MEANS `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
`barred` MEANS `regulation 4 bars the service`

§§ `J5: row 5, registration for a theoretical exam`

#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 5` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 5` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 5` EQUALS `not barred`
-- The fee row 5 implies (273, the draft's 2(a)) is reproduced by the draft only.
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `draft` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 5`
#ASSERT NOT (`the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 5`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 5`)

§§ `J6: row 6, registration for a practical exam`

#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 6` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 6` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 6` EQUALS `not barred`
-- 194 in all three.
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `draft` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 6`
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 6`
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 6`

§§ `J7: row 7, an appeal with payment of 40`

-- The draft: either exam.
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam` EQUALS `not barred`
-- As made: an objection to the practical exam (40 fixed, 40 paid).
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam` EQUALS `not barred`
-- As amended: an objection to the theoretical exam (40 fixed, 40 paid).
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam` EQUALS `not barred`
-- As amended an objection to a practical exam has no fee at all: examined, and nothing implied by the 40 is reproduced.
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT NOT (`the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam`)
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam`

§§ `J8: row 8, registration for an exam without payment`

-- A practical exam: refused in all three.
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a practical exam` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a practical exam` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a practical exam` EQUALS `barred`
-- A theoretical exam: refused in the draft and as amended; NOT refused as made, which fixes no fee for it.
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a theoretical exam` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a theoretical exam` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a theoretical exam` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT NOT (`the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a theoretical exam`)
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `SimpLEX row 8, a theoretical exam`

§§ `J9: the worked example, a theoretical exam not paid for`

#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `the SimpLEX worked example` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `the SimpLEX worked example` EQUALS `not barred`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `the SimpLEX worked example` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `draft` `, reading the case as` `draft reg 4 as made` `, the case being` `the SimpLEX worked example`
#ASSERT NOT (`the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `as made` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `the SimpLEX worked example`)
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `as amended` `, reading the case as` `taken` `, the case being` `the SimpLEX worked example`
